Package: akari-base
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, base-files (>= 13)
Recommends: akari-archive-keyring
Description: Akari OS system identity
 Makes a Debian system an Akari OS: /usr/lib/os-release says ID=akari,
 ID_LIKE=debian (so programs know it is Debian underneath), the console
 greets with Akari OS, GRUB wears Akari's theme, and dpkg knows the origin
 Akari.
 .
 Debian's os-release stays on the system, moved aside (dpkg-divert) and
 back in place when this package goes. Debian's /etc/issue is not touched:
 the console's agetty reads Akari's issue instead.
